&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager - Accounts, you will be responsible for the strategy, roadmap, and execution of Alpaca&#39;s core account management and identity verification systems. You will be the voice of our partners, working to create a flexible and compliant global account infrastructure. This role is critical to enabling financial institutions around the world to seamlessly and securely onboard and manage their end-users. You will work closely with engineering, legal, compliance, and business development teams to navigate the complexities of different jurisdictions and deliver a world-class account experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Things You Get To Do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the product vision, strategy, and roadmap for Alpaca&#39;s account opening and identity verification services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the lifecycle of various account structures, including fully disclosed, omnibus, and omnibus with sub-accounting, to meet the diverse needs of our global B2B clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and enhance features such as the ability to open accounts for entities, create sub-accounts for distinct trading strategies, and manage multiple account types (e.g., self-directed, robo, retirement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the strategy for KYC and identity verification, supporting various models from partner-led KYC to integrated solutions with third-party providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with legal, compliance, and regional business teams to navigate the complexities of different jurisdictions, ensuring our account systems meet local licensing, data management, and financial requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author detailed product requirement documents (PRDs) and user stories to ensure clarity and alignment across all teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with go-to-market teams to enable adoption of new account features and onboarding flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and analyze key metrics such as onboarding success rates, account funding times, and KYC pass-through rates to measure success and identify areas for improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Are (Must-Haves):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of product management experience, with a focus on B2B, fintech, or complex platform products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with products related to user onboarding, identity verification (KYC/AML), or account management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of the operational and regulatory complexities in financial services, especially concerning client onboarding and account lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to understand complex technical and business requirements and work effectively with engineering, legal, and compliance teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a proven track record of leading cross-functional teams and influencing stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven mindset with experience using analytics tools to track product performance and make informed decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine passion for financial markets and a strong desire to build products that empower developers and democratize access to financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an agile development environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Might Be (Nice-to-Haves):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience working in the fintech or brokerage industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a globally distributed, remote-first company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with different brokerage account structures (e.g., omnibus, fully disclosed)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with global identity verification providers and regulatory technology (RegTech)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.alpaca.markets/disclosures/AlpacaRecruitmentPrivacyPolicy.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Energy Exemplar&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In an era where the world is rapidly advancing towards a cleaner future through decarbonization, Energy Exemplar’s mission lies in ‘Empowering Transformative Energy Decisions’. Founded in 1999 in Adelaide, Australia, our award-winning software portfolio encompassing the modeling and simulation platform PLEXOS®, Aurora, and Adapt2, is trusted by innovative organizations across the globe. Through our technology and people, we strive to enable stakeholders from across the entire energy value chain to revolutionize the energy ecosystem and to collaboratively plan and execute for a sustainable energy future with unprecedented clarity, speed, and innovation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our impact is global and is being recognized across the industry. Some of our recent accolades include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;SaaS Company of the Year (2025) – Global Business Tech Awards.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Environmental Impact Award (2025) – E+E Leaders Awards.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;IPPAI (Independent Power Producers Association of India) Power Awards (2025) - Winners&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Finalist: Platts Global Energy Awards (2024) – Grid Edge category&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Finalist: Reuters Global Energy Transition Awards (2024) – Technologies of Change&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Top 50 Marketing Team (2024) – Voted by the public at the ICON Awards.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Energy Exemplar is growing fast around 30% year on year and, that growth is driven by how we work. We trust our team to deliver great results from wherever they work best, whether that’s at home, in the office, or on the move.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a global team that values ownership, integrity, and innovation. You’ll be supported to balance work and life in a way that works for you, and empowered to take initiative, solve problems, and make an impact, regardless of your background, location, or role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our four core values, Customer Success, One Global Team, Integrity &amp;amp; Ownership, and Innovation Excellence aren’t just words. They show up in how we collaborate, how we solve, and how we grow together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Energy Market Analyst – Trading, you will sit within Energy Exemplar’s EMEA Solutions team, acting as a key technical partner to power trading customers across the region. You will combine deep knowledge of electricity markets and fundamental energy market modelling with an understanding of trading desk workflows to help customers use PLEXOS to support commercial and trading decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will work closely with power trading organisations, the EMEA Sales team, Solutions colleagues and Product teams. You will support customers across the full lifecycle from pre-sales demonstrations and proof-of-concept engagements through to model implementation, onboarding, optimisation and ongoing customer success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be accountable for delivering high quality modelling solutions that address customer needs, translating complex market and modelling concepts into actionable insights, and identifying opportunities to improve how trading organisations use fundamental modelling in their decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly collaborative and customer facing role, with the opportunity to work with leading organisations across EMEA, contribute to thought leadership in power trading, and influence the continued development of PLEXOS for trading applications. The role can be based from Energy Exemplar’s London office or remotely within Europe, with international travel across EMEA as required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted technical advisor to power trading customers, developing strong relationships and understanding their commercial objectives, workflows and modelling requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, development and delivery of fundamental energy market modelling solutions using PLEXOS and related technologies to support trading and portfolio decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with customers to analyse modelling outputs, validate assumptions and data, and continuously improve models to ensure they provide relevant and actionable market insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the full customer lifecycle, including requirements gathering, onboarding, training, troubleshooting, model optimisation and ongoing technical support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the EMEA Sales team on prospective customer engagements, including technical demonstrations, proof-of-concept studies, presentations and responses to detailed functional and technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use scripting, automation, APIs, CLI tools and cloud-based environments to develop efficient modelling workflows and integrate PLEXOS into customer processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product and Solutions teams to communicate customer needs, identify opportunities for product improvement and contribute to the development of trading-focused capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market research and develop original analysis on emerging trends in power markets and trading, contributing to thought leadership, webinars, conferences and customer-facing content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple customer engagements and priorities across EMEA, balancing delivery, stakeholder management and commercial requirements in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel internationally across the EMEA region when required to support customers, sales opportunities, training and industry engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Requirements &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7+ years of experience in energy markets, with a strong understanding of electricity market fundamentals, energy economics, power system operations and/or energy trading.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience using fundamental energy market supply and demand models, including optimisation, unit commitment or dispatch modelling, to analyse electricity markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of power trading and electricity market dynamics, including how modelling can support price forecasting, market analysis, portfolio decisions, risk assessment and trading strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python or similar scripting skills, with experience using code to automate analytical or modelling workflows and work with data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret complex modelling outputs, challenge assumptions and translate analysis into clear commercial insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to build credibility and rapport with both technical and commercial audiences, including traders and other senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, customer requirements and competing priorities in a fast-paced, customer-facing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A tertiary qualification in Electrical Engineering, Energy Economics, Operations Research, or a related discipline, ideally with a focus on electricity systems or energy markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired but not required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hands on experience with&amp;nbsp;PLEXOS or another commercial energy market optimisation platform such as EPSI, BID3, Antares, SDDP or PROMOD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience working within or closely with a power trading desk, including exposure to day-ahead, intraday, balancing or other electricity markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying fundamental modelling to cross-border flows, congestion analysis, ancillary services, capacity markets, portfolio optimisation, VaR or hedging strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with APIs, CLI tools and cloud-based computation environments, particularly where these have been used to integrate energy market models into automated trading or analytical workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Energy Exemplar is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all team members. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, identities, and abilities. Please let us know if you require accommodations at any stage of the recruitment process—we&#39;re here to support you in showcasing your full potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Energy Exemplar respects your privacy and is committed to protecting the personal data you share during the recruitment process. This Candidate &lt;a&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; explains how we collect, use, and protect your personal information when you apply for a role with us.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fastly helps people stay better connected with the things they love. Fastly’s edge cloud platform enables customers to create great digital experiences quickly, securely, and reliably by processing, serving, and securing our customers’ applications as close to their end-users as possible — at the edge of the Internet. The platform is designed to take advantage of the modern internet, to be programmable, and to support agile software development. Fastly’s customers include many of the world’s most prominent companies, including GitHub, Yelp, Paramount, and JetBlue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building a more trustworthy Internet. Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;The Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fastly is looking for a Senior Enterprise Customer Success Manager to join our team in the UK. In this role, you will be a primary driver of our Customer Success Charter, maintaining a laser focus on renewals, retention, and expansion. You will serve as a trusted advisor to a portfolio of Enterprise customers, nurturing relationships from the C-suite down to technical stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for building high-value account strategies, driving product adoption, and mitigating risk to ensure long-term customer health. Success in this role is measured by your ability to deliver a &quot;net positive&quot; impact on our regional revenue and the measurable value we provide to our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account Planning &amp;amp; Strategy: Document and execute comprehensive strategy plans within your &quot;node.&quot; This includes relationship mapping, identifying revenue opportunities, and driving adoption of our sponsorship programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account Expansion &amp;amp; Lead Gen: Expand executive reach through Executive Business Reviews (EBRs) and value-based reporting. You will map parent-subsidiary accounts to unlock new business units and drive deeper product integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product Adoption: Ensure full adoption of existing and new product introductions by aligning Fastly’s solutions with specific customer priorities and pain points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Churn Prevention: Act as a trusted advisor to create &quot;sticky&quot; relationships. You will leverage executive relationships to nurture accounts at the decision-maker level and introduce product solutions that proactively close customer gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Renewals: Execute a &quot;give-to-get&quot; renewal strategy to achieve net-positive re-rate percentages. You will negotiate logo rights to enhance brand positioning and manage terms to ensure favorable outcomes for both Fastly and customers mainly across the e-commerce vertical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration: Partner closely with Sales, Sales Engineering, and Marketing to provide the &quot;Voice of the Customer&quot; (VOC) feedback, ensuring our product roadmap aligns with regional needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: Proven Account Management and strategic Customer Success experience, ideally within the CDN, PaaS, or Cybersecurity industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Mindset: A track record of driving revenue through up-selling and cross-selling, with the ability to navigate complex &quot;parent-subsidiary&quot; account structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationship Builder: Confident in managing C-level relationships and running high-impact customer meetings, workshops, and roundtables. This includes a proven track record of navigating complex Enterprise organizations to grow account relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Literacy: A technical background is highly valued; you should be able to align technical concepts with business value and customer goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Excellence: Highly organized with a strong attention to detail and strong project management skills. The individual will demonstrate the ability to work autonomously in a fast-paced, remote environment. A self starter mindset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication: Exceptional verbal and written communication skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Success: Delight customers by demonstrating responsiveness and ensuring timely responses across account activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Work Hours &amp;amp; Location&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hours: Core business hours&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: This position is a hybrid role and open to candidates residing in the following locations: London&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel: Periodic travel across the UK and Europe is required to engage with customers in person.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fastly is an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Fastly?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We have a huge impact.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Fastly is a small company with a big reach. Not only do&lt;a class=&quot;external-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.fastly.com/customers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;our customers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;have a tremendous user base, but we also support a growing number of&lt;a class=&quot;external-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.fastly.com/open-source/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;open source projects and initiatives&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;Outside of code, employees are encouraged to share causes close to their heart with others so we can help lend a supportive hand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We value diversity.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Growing and maintaining our inclusive and diverse team matters to us. We are committed to being a company where our employees feel comfortable bringing their authentic selves to work and have the ability to be successful -- every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are passionate.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Fastly is chock full of passionate people and we’re not ‘one size fits all’. Fastly employs authors, pilots, skiers, parents (of humans and animals), makeup geeks, coffee connoisseurs, and more. We love employees for who they are and what they are passionate about.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re always looking for humble, sharp, and creative folks to join the Fastly team. If you think you might be a fit please apply!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; A fully completed application and resume or CV are required when applying.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;All job applications must be submitted through our official careers site at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fastly.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fastly.com/about/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;. We will never request sensitive information, such as your Social Security number, bank account or credit card information during the application process. All official communication will come from an @&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://fastly.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;fastly.com&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; or @&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://recruiting.fastly.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;recruiting.fastly.com&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; email address. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Fastly is committed to ensuring equal employment opportunity and to providing employees with a safe and welcoming work environment free of discrimination and harassment. Our employment decisions are based on business needs, job requirements and individual qualifications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ancestry, color, family or medical care leave, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, medical condition, national origin, family or parental status, physical or mental disability, political affiliation, protected veteran status, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations and ordinances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Consistent with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and federal or state disability laws, Fastly will provide reasonable accommodations for applicants and employees with disabilities. If reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other benefits and privileges of employment, please contact your Recruiter, or the Fastly Employee Relations team at &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a ----- style=&quot;font-weight: ----- style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; or 501-287-4901.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fastly collects and processes personal data submitted by job applicants in accordance with our&lt;a class=&quot;external-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.fastly.com/privacy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;. Please see our&lt;a class=&quot;external-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.fastly.com/privacy-job-applicants&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;privacy notice for job applicants&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Anaplan, we are a team of innovators focused on optimizing business decision-making through our leading AI-infused scenario planning and analysis platform so our customers can outpace their competition and the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What unites Anaplanners across teams and geographies is our collective commitment to our customers’ success and to our Winning Culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Our customers rank among the who’s who in the Fortune 50. Coca-Cola, LinkedIn, Adobe, LVMH and Bayer are just a few of the 2,400+ global companies who rely on our best-in-class platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Our Winning Culture is the engine that drives our teams of innovators. We champion diversity of thought and ideas, we behave like leaders regardless of title, we are committed to achieving ambitious goals, and we love celebrating&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;our wins – big and small.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supported by operating principles of being strategy-led, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anaplan.com/careers/&quot;&gt;values&lt;/a&gt;-based and disciplined in execution, you’ll be inspired, connected, developed and rewarded here. Everything that makes you unique is welcome; join us and let’s build what’s next - together!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a dynamic and hands-on Senior Manager to lead Anaplan’s Technical Content team – the group responsible for Anapedia (our product documentation), the Anaplan Planual (our modeling best-practice standard), documentation for the Anaplan Applications portfolio, and supporting disciplines such as localisation. This is a working manager role: you will lead a team of roughly 18 people organised into three sub-teams, while staying close enough to the content itself to set direction, raise the bar, and jump in where it matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is not satisfied with how technical content has “always been done.” You will be expected to question established processes, modernise our content operations, and champion the use of AI technologies to scale content creation, maintenance, and localisation – without compromising the accuracy and trust our customers place in Anapedia and the Planual.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
