&lt;h3&gt;About Dwelly&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dwelly is building the AI operating system for residential lettings. Its growing network of agencies provides its AI with real-world data, continuous feedback, and control over complete workflows, making exceptional service the standard for landlords and tenants. Today, Dwelly operates more than 15,000 properties and $470 million in GMV, making it one of the UK’s ten largest lettings operators. The company has raised $263 million.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re a fast-growing, product-focused company, backed by top-tier investors and led by a team with deep experience in real estate, technology, and operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Position Summary&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly talented and hands-on Senior Product Designer to help shape the experience across the full set of Dwelly products (Tenant Find, Property Management, Payments, CRM) and the internal back-office tools that power them. This role involves deeply understanding our user personas (Tenant, Landlord, Maintenance Contractor, Dwelly Agent) and designing for both the customer-facing portals and the operational tools our agents use every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Given the early stage of the business, our current products are hyper-functional but quite basic — an &quot;MVP&quot; that prioritises getting the job done across all domains. You&#39;ll work closely with product and engineering to take these to the next level: bringing clarity, usability, and craft to data-dense, workflow-heavy internal tools, and building genuinely good experiences for tenants and landlords. You&#39;ll also help establish the basic building blocks of design at Dwelly — a shared design system, patterns, and a lightweight design process — from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our current development team is a team of 5, a few analysts, and one product designer. You&#39;ll join a small, fast-moving product team and have an outsized impact on how the whole product looks, feels, and works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User Research &amp;amp; Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with product to understand user pain points across all personas — tenants, landlords, maintenance contractors, and internal agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn qualitative and quantitative insights into design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an advocate for usability and the end user within the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. End-to-End Product Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design flows, wireframes, and high-fidelity UIs for both customer-facing products (tenant and landlord portals) and internal back-office tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for data-dense, workflow-heavy operational products where clarity and efficiency matter more than decoration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design process from concept and prototyping through to polished, build-ready specs, and iterate after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Design Across the Product Suite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring consistency and quality across Tenant Find, Property Management, Payments, and the communications/portal layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineers and product managers to translate requirements into shippable design, balancing craft with speed and technical feasibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Design System &amp;amp; Process Building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain a shared design system, component library, and reusable patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce lightweight design workflows, documentation, and review/handoff practices suited to an early-stage team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Qualifications &amp;amp; Preferred Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience&amp;nbsp;in product design, with a strong portfolio spanning both complex/operational tools and consumer-facing products. Comfortable in early-stage, low-structure environments as well as more structured, product-led settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong interaction and visual design skills; systems thinking; exceptional attention to detail; able to design for complexity and make it feel simple. Excellent communication and collaboration skills across product and engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In step with recent technology advancements: &lt;strong&gt;can prototype and ship designs quickly and independently with the help of AI.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing operational, back-office, or B2B tools where efficiency and workflow are central — ideally in tech-enabled or operational businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or contributing to a design system from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sense of ownership, a &quot;get things done&quot; attitude, and excellent attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary with the potential for equity options based on performance, recognising exceptional contributions to our integration success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What is it like being a Dwell-er?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Feel free to check out &lt;a href=&quot;https://docsend.com/view/7v8gwrjaky7mn895&quot;&gt;Dwelly Core Principles&lt;/a&gt;. That’s about what we believe in, how we operate and make decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What we offer is not a fancy office or a static workplace. Instead, this is solving one of worlds’ most complex problems in the largest consumer industry in the world (residential rentals), to improve the experience for &amp;gt;30% of households (&amp;gt;5M in the UK, and &amp;gt;100M including EU and US) that live in rental homes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is about disrupting the largest, most antiquated industry in the world, with one of the strongest operational and technical teams that exist in the UK and the EU. We work hard, and we shoot for extremely ambitious results. But we want people to be proud of what they’ve built and be able to look back and say one day “hell yeah, that was me that did it all”.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer obsession rather than competitive focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for invention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long-term thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;556&quot; data-end=&quot;829&quot;&gt;By applying for this position, you consent to the processing and storage of your personal data for recruitment purposes for up to 365 days, in accordance with our data retention policy and applicable data protection laws.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:280}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SharkNinja&amp;nbsp;is a global product design and technology company, with a diversified portfolio of 5-star rated lifestyle solutions that positively&amp;nbsp;impact&amp;nbsp;people’s lives in homes around the world. &lt;strong&gt;Powered by two trusted, global brands, Shark and Ninja&lt;/strong&gt;, the company has a proven&amp;nbsp;track record&amp;nbsp;of bringing disruptive innovation to market and developing one consumer product after another has allowed&amp;nbsp;SharkNinja&amp;nbsp;to enter multiple product categories, driving significant growth and market share gains. Headquartered in Needham, Massachusetts with more than&amp;nbsp;4,100&amp;nbsp;associates, the company’s products are sold at key retailers, online and offline, and through distributors around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI at SharkNinja &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SharkNinja, we’re building an AI-native culture. We’re not waiting for the future; we’re creating it. Our people are expected to experiment boldly, adopt new tools, and continuously raise what’s possible to create meaningful impact for our consumers. If you believe the best way to do your job hasn’t been invented yet, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Senior Product Integrity Engineer&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About SharkNinja&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SharkNinja is a global product design and technology company with a diversified portfolio of lifestyle solutions that positively impact people’s lives in homes around the world. Powered by two trusted global brands, Shark and Ninja, we bring disruptive innovation to market across multiple product categories, creating products that consumers love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI at SharkNinja&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SharkNinja, we’re building an AI-native culture. We’re not waiting for the future; we’re creating it. Our people are expected to experiment boldly, adopt new tools and continuously raise what’s possible to create meaningful impact for our consumers. If you believe the best way to do your job hasn’t been invented yet, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a technically strong, proactive and detail-oriented &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Integrity Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our UK team, with a focus on design assurance, engineering validation and product quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Embedded within the New Product Development (NPD) process, you will take ownership of product integrity activities from concept through to production launch, ensuring quality, safety, reliability and consumer expectations are built into the design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with Engineering, Industrial Design, Product Development, Manufacturing and Supply Chain to lead risk assessment and validation activities. You will use engineering judgement, test evidence and consumer insights to challenge designs, resolve risks and influence decisions at critical development milestones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role offers broad cross-functional exposure and the opportunity to directly influence whether our products deliver SharkNinja’s 5-star quality standard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design assurance and engineering validation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead product integrity input into design reviews, Design Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (DFMEA), design verification and validation planning (DVP&amp;amp;R), and safety reviews throughout the NPD lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the development and delivery of risk-based verification and validation plans, establishing clear test methods, acceptance criteria and evidence requirements aligned with product specifications and applicable UK, European and other target-market requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Challenge design assumptions and assess product performance, reliability, robustness and foreseeable use conditions, ensuring risks are understood and addressed before tooling and production release.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evaluate engineering changes for their impact on quality, safety and performance, defining appropriate revalidation requirements to prevent regression.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Review and approve quality-related manufacturing and test documentation within your remit, ensuring requirements are clearly translated into production controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to Design for Manufacture (DFM) reviews, assessing tolerances, process capability and potential sources of manufacturing variation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide evidence-based recommendations on product readiness, escalating unresolved risks and driving corrective action ahead of development milestones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional leadership and quality governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent product integrity within cross-functional NPD teams, translating consumer expectations and quality requirements into practical engineering decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead quality risk and action reviews, establishing clear ownership, priorities and closure criteria.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with Manufacturing, Supply Chain and suppliers to define process controls, quality gates and production acceptance criteria ahead of mass production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead technical investigation of issues identified during prototype, pilot and pre-production builds, coordinating root-cause analysis and verifying corrective action effectiveness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Challenge supplier 8D investigations and corrective action proposals, ensuring conclusions are supported by robust evidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive corrective and preventive action (CAPA) activities addressing design and process gaps, tracking actions through to verified closure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide technical guidance to colleagues and support the development of consistent product integrity practices across programmes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data analysis and continuous improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Analyse validation results, build data, test failures and relevant field performance insights to identify emerging risks and prioritise improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define and monitor quality metrics, validation coverage and acceptance criteria throughout the development cycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply lessons from existing products to new designs, strengthening test coverage and preventing repeat failures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Improve validation methods and pre-production quality processes, addressing systemic gaps with sustainable solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Communicate validation status, residual risks and corrective action progress clearly to senior management and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A degree in Mechanical Engineering, Product Design Engineering, Quality Engineering or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Substantial relevant engineering experience, typically gained over five or more years, with demonstrated ownership of design verification, validation or product integrity activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Practical experience leading DFMEA, DVP&amp;amp;R, technical design reviews and engineering change assessments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A strong understanding of product development lifecycles, design and document control, and verification and validation methodologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience translating product requirements and engineering risks into measurable test plans and acceptance criteria.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong technical problem-solving and root-cause analysis skills, with the ability to interpret test data and assess corrective action effectiveness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional teams, challenge technical decisions constructively and drive issues through to resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clear communication skills, including the ability to explain technical risks and recommendations to engineering teams and senior stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Confidence managing multiple programmes and competing priorities in a fast-paced development environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Excel, Word and PowerPoint, with experience using data to support engineering decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively across teams, regions and supplier partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience developing consumer appliances, electromechanical products or other high-volume consumer goods.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working within rapid NPD cycles and supporting products through tooling, pilot builds and production launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of reliability engineering, accelerated life testing, statistical analysis or Design of Experiments (DOE).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with supplier quality processes, Production Part Approval Process (PPAP), process capability assessment and incoming quality controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understanding of applicable product safety standards and UK and European product compliance requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience incorporating human factors, usability and foreseeable misuse into product validation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working with international manufacturing partners and suppliers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role may require travel within the UK and internationally to support development builds, manufacturing sites and supplier activities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
